# Zulip/secrets/zuliprc.example
#
# The file broker's Zulip credentials (I-ZU-10, IN-5.17, broker.md §7.2). Copy to
# Zulip/secrets/zuliprc — no `.example` suffix — once the bot exists, and mount it
# read-only into the Workcenter container from the root compose
# (production.md §11.1 lists the tree that must be backed up, secrets included).
#
# Format: Zulip's own `zuliprc` (python-zulip-api), one [api] section. The broker
# uses `email` + `key` as HTTP Basic for POST /api/v1/user_uploads,
# POST /api/v1/messages and GET /user_uploads/... (IN-5.15, IN-5.16).
#
# The key cannot be generated offline: create the bot in Zulip under
# Settings → Bots (a generic bot is enough), copy its API key here, and subscribe
# the bot to the channel that the "send file to Zulip" action targets. A bot
# without that subscription fails the flow with a permission error, not a
# transport error.
#
# What this credential deliberately cannot do: PATCH /api/v1/settings is
# @human_users_only, so the bot key cannot change anyone's appearance or language
# (IN-5.23). Those writes use the user's own key, which is the design (BR-6.3).
[api]
email=file-broker-bot@example.com
key=REPLACE_WITH_THE_BOT_API_KEY_FROM_ZULIP
site=https://chat.example.com
